      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given the information, if the fluid is clean, a solenoid issue may indeed be responsible for the fluctuations in hydraulic pressure – these components act as switches that control the flow of hydraulic fluid, and wear or electrical issues can disrupt the hydraulic pressure consistency. A sensor could also be faulty, causing uneven operation and pressure readings. Before resorting to a full pan or valve body replacement, inspecting and potentially replacing the solenoids and associated sensors can be a more economical approach. Be sure to use the manufacturer's repair manual for guidance to ensure all steps are accurate before disassembly.",
